From 8ec99909183e04921bd63c8c9a19d07541860bc9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Pete 'TFNG' Copeland <petec4244@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 17:06:23 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] feat(renderer, layout): colour emoji on Windows

RustKit on Windows painted no emoji at all. The colour path (RGBA atlas,
blit pipeline, is_emoji routing) was already wired for macOS; the Windows
side had `let raster = None`, the grayscale fallback then asked Segoe UI or
Arial for a glyph they do not have, and the character painted nothing.
image-gallery's eight "photos" are emoji on gradients: 1.13 of its 1.59
points on Windows were the missing glyphs. about, card-grid, sticky-scroll,
chrome_rustkit and settings carry emoji too.

Three pieces, all cfg(windows) or platform-neutral; macOS is untouched:

1. rustkit-renderer glyph.rs: rasterize_glyph_directwrite_color draws the
   character from Segoe UI Emoji (Chrome's Windows emoji face) through
   Direct2D's DrawTextLayout with ENABLE_COLOR_FONT into a WIC bitmap,
   crops it to its ink, and returns premultiplied RGBA with the same
   bitmap-edge contract as the grayscale rasterizer. Direct2D renders every
   colour format the OS knows, including the COLRv1 paint trees Segoe UI
   Emoji ships on Windows 11, so the artwork matches Chrome's.
   IDWriteFactory2::TranslateColorGlyphRun was tried first: it yields only
   the flat COLRv0 layers, which differ from Chrome's COLRv1 rendering by
   more than the missing glyph did (image-gallery 1.59 -> 1.73).

2. rustkit-text: is_emoji moves from the macOS module to a shared emoji.rs
   (re-exported from macos for existing callers); the renderer's is_color
   check now runs on Windows too.

3. rustkit-layout text.rs, the Windows shaper: a character the primary
   face has no glyph for took the primary face's .notdef advance, and
   U+FE0F took a real width. Chrome measures the emoji with the face it
   falls back to and gives selectors zero advance; with the wrong width
   every emoji was centred 8 px right of Chrome's. Emoji now take Segoe UI
   Emoji's advance and default-ignorable code points take none.

Windows parity board (Mac in parentheses): image-gallery 1.59 -> 0.51
(0.52), about 3.98 -> 3.45 (3.75), card-grid 1.00 -> 0.76 (1.29),
chrome_rustkit 1.23 -> 0.74 (1.13), sticky-scroll 0.79 -> 0.45 (0.66).
Tests: rustkit-text 55/0, rustkit-renderer 85/0, rustkit-layout 563/0
including a Windows test for the advances.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CjYMYAQpVR2s8jLuPgBpnU
